    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0176" n="88" xml:id="pg88"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Hale.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 111.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm the Department’s telegram to you
                    of the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith original papers which the Red Star Line, through its counsel,
                    Mr. S. C. Neale, has submitted to the Department.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d54-f1"/>
                    They appear to make out a prima facie showing of discrimination against the Red
                    Star Line in favor of the Cunard Line by the Hungarian authorities, and the
                    Department feels justified in instructing you to use your good offices in behalf
                    of the American interests discriminated against to obtain proper relief for
                    them.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
